# TypeORM Migrations

> **DDL only. Always include down(). Test both directions.**

---

## 📝 Template

```typescript
import { MigrationInterface, QueryRunner } from 'typeorm';

export class AddColumnName1770300000000 implements MigrationInterface {
  name = 'AddColumnName1770300000000';

  public async up(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    await queryRunner.query(`
      ALTER TABLE "table_name"
      ADD COLUMN "column_name" varchar(50) DEFAULT 'value'
    `);
  }

  public async down(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    await queryRunner.query(`
      ALTER TABLE "table_name"
      DROP COLUMN "column_name"
    `);
  }
}
```

---

## ⚡ Common Patterns

```sql
-- Add column
ALTER TABLE "t" ADD COLUMN "c" type DEFAULT value;

-- Add index (partial for soft delete)
CREATE INDEX "idx_t_c" ON "t" ("c") WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;

-- Add trigger for updated_at
CREATE TRIGGER update_t_updated_at
  BEFORE UPDATE ON "t"
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();
```

---

## 🚫 NEVER

```
❌ DML in migrations (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)
❌ Skip down() method
❌ Modify existing migration files
❌ Hardcode data — use seeds
```
